DESCRIPTION:Amid minimum wage protests by garment workers\, thirteen garmen
 t factories in Gazipur shut indefinitely under the Bangladesh Labour Act (
 2006) and over 50 remain closed in Savar and Ashulia\, while 48 platoons o
 f the Border Guard\, Ansar\, and Special Response Battalion deploy across 
 industrial zones in Dhaka\, Gazipur\, and Narayanganj.\n\nProtest: Banglad
 esh\nReported by The Business Standard: https://www.tbsnews.net/economy/rm
 g/13-factories-shut-indefinitely-gazipur-amid-labour-unrest-holiday-declar
